The system's dialog for choosing where to save a file. It asks before
replacing a file that exists, so the path it returns can be written.

It blocks until answered and has to run on the UI thread, which is where
event handlers such as `on_click` run.

```no_run
use ravenrs_platform_native::SaveDialog;

let chosen = SaveDialog::new("Contas.pdf").title("Exportar").filter("PDF", &["pdf"]).ask();
if let Some(path) = chosen {
    std::fs::write(path, b"...")?;
}
# Ok::<(), std::io::Error>(())
```

748.docs:
Who the app is to the system, for finding its icon and its menu entry.

On Linux the id is what ties the window to the app's `.desktop` file. Wayland
has no way for a window to carry an icon: GNOME shows the one in the
`.desktop` file whose name, without the extension, is the window's id. On
X11 the id must match the file's `StartupWMClass`.

```
use ravenrs_platform_native::AppIdentity;

// For a file named `notes.desktop`.
let identity = AppIdentity::new("notes");
```

320.docs:
The system's dialog for choosing a file to open.

It blocks until answered and has to run on the UI thread, which is where
event handlers such as `on_click` run.

```no_run
use ravenrs_platform_native::OpenDialog;

let chosen = OpenDialog::new().title("Abrir").filter("Texto", &["txt"]).ask();
if let Some(path) = chosen {
    let text = std::fs::read_to_string(path)?;
}
# Ok::<(), std::io::Error>(())
```

